CLUB AFFILIATION

Become Part of OCRA

The Obstacle Course Racing Association of Ireland (OCRA ÉIREANN) wants to build a national network of obstacle racing clubs working together to develop the sport throughout Ireland.

Club affiliation creates a formal relationship between an OCR club and OCRA and allows clubs to become part of the wider national structure of obstacle sport.

Why Affiliate With OCRA?

Affiliation is intended to help clubs connect with the national development of OCR and access opportunities that would be difficult to build independently.

Depending on the current OCRA affiliation programme, support and opportunities may include:

- Recognition as an OCRA Affiliated Club
- Inclusion in the OCRA Club Directory
- Promotion through OCRA channels
- Access to coaching development opportunities
- Access to Technical Official education
- Club development support
- Information about events and competitions
- National Championship information
- International qualification information
- Opportunities to collaborate with OCRA programmes and events
- Connections with other clubs and training facilities
- Participation in the wider development of obstacle sport in Ireland

Building a National Club Network

A strong national sport needs strong local clubs.

OCRA wants affiliated clubs to remain independent organisations while also being able to work together on areas where national coordination provides value.

This may include:

- Athlete development
- Coach education
- Youth development
- Competition
- Club events
- Technical standards
- Safeguarding
- Community programmes
- National initiatives

Who Can Apply?

OCR clubs and established obstacle training communities operating in Ireland can apply for affiliation.

The exact affiliation requirements will depend on the structure and activities of the club.

Clubs may be asked to provide information such as:

- Club name
- Location
- Club contact details
- Club structure
- Training activities
- Coaches
- Safeguarding arrangements, where applicable
- Membership information
- Relevant club policies

Club Responsibilities

Affiliated clubs are expected to operate in a way that supports safe, fair and inclusive participation in obstacle sport.

This includes respecting applicable OCRA policies and maintaining appropriate standards within club activities.

Where clubs provide youth activities, additional safeguarding requirements will apply.

Affiliation and Independence

OCRA affiliation does not mean that OCRA operates or controls the day-to-day activities of an affiliated club.

Clubs remain responsible for their own management, activities, finances and members.

Affiliation provides a recognised relationship with OCRA and a way for clubs to participate in the wider national development of the sport.

Interested in Affiliation?

If your club is interested in becoming affiliated with OCRA, contact us to discuss the current affiliation process.

New clubs are also welcome to contact OCRA before applying if they would like guidance on becoming ready for affiliation.

